{"agent_id":"pp3g-3bc4-investigate-issue-144-tier-1-experiment-verify-fafe","agent_seq":9,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:08:59.189418831Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"951b3b57-44f1-4503-9404-6cb182065dd1","comment_uuid":"eba41ab3-d778-4b33-bd37-e408a5d4fe06","author":"pp3g-3bc4-investigate-issue-144-tier-1-experiment-verify-fafe","content":"Plan: (1) verify config propagation via log loading-lines + launch chain source; (2) verify chunkTimeout implementation in opencode 1.18.11 source (wrapSSE guard); (3) controlled repro with fake hanging SSE server; (4) verdict with file:function evidence. Key hypothesis forming: wrapSSE only wraps content-type text/event-stream — non-SSE responses bypass chunkTimeout entirely.","created_at":"2026-08-03T18:08:59.176848616Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:fmLzQ5FXIztSEmsIH9qJZbpnPkgYSIkTl4JepA/OauE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgt+/Xfi/pqw4EWd/WlHR/LiU5R4t7k+H5zYx8tl1YnFwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAXxJTa7mgi+NGpp9A8bgsikUyHEIDHuYVm0ggDBfDAwFT8YA1LqMWmSdKBjqESGNs0oWZIICc5sVuOex0Aw2xBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:fmLzQ5FXIztSEmsIH9qJZbpnPkgYSIkTl4JepA/OauE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgt+/Xfi/pqw4EWd/WlHR/LiU5R4t7k+H5zYx8tl1YnFwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI+75btF7KoJRRhMSkyWuGOjWGxG93WDu8rAg2ppwx0fIREMPtKj/G6MtzSX2ViMGudaNwwno+FJ81JoKg0Kiw8="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-3bc4-investigate-issue-144-tier-1-experiment-verify-fafe","agent_seq":10,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:09:07.138464210Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"951b3b57-44f1-4503-9404-6cb182065dd1","comment_uuid":"aca1b0a5-07ee-483e-bd5c-52e96f2bb040","author":"pp3g-3bc4-investigate-issue-144-tier-1-experiment-verify-fafe","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=plan posted; config propagation CONFIRMED (both hung sessions loaded ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json at launch); chunkTimeout IS implemented in opencode 1.18.11 but wrapSSE has content-type guard; controlled repro shows chunkTimeout fires on text/event-stream (silent retries, zero ERROR) but is BYPASSED on application/json (infinite hang, zero retries) next=write verdict comment with evidence","created_at":"2026-08-03T18:09:07.130997106Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:fmLzQ5FXIztSEmsIH9qJZbpnPkgYSIkTl4JepA/OauE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgt+/Xfi/pqw4EWd/WlHR/LiU5R4t7k+H5zYx8tl1YnFwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA77PMrSvQMORnYswrtpOdERBs1jzNsPo5LDnPvj0BJAzdMB54YqP5mwX0iJAN593Hs50Bv3MNGPH/D70Oi3a3DQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:fmLzQ5FXIztSEmsIH9qJZbpnPkgYSIkTl4JepA/OauE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgt+/Xfi/pqw4EWd/WlHR/LiU5R4t7k+H5zYx8tl1YnFwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF+r4hP7P0U7vJUivVgB89tPf5z/+HcOy0QWj//EdTRjIcwe2rZQ13/Yw/R9A6CtuWv9iUWdr49Fr38iQHa7MQw="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-3bc4-investigate-issue-144-tier-1-experiment-verify-fafe","agent_seq":11,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:11:07.127862130Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"951b3b57-44f1-4503-9404-6cb182065dd1","comment_uuid":"d092b794-70d7-4780-8a54-22331d8a1d3b","author":"pp3g-3bc4-investigate-issue-144-tier-1-experiment-verify-fafe","content":"## VERDICT: The current chunkTimeout config does NOT protect against the silent-hang failure\n\n**Answer: NO — the config as written (timeout=3600000, headerTimeout=300000, chunkTimeout=300000) does NOT protect. The chunkTimeout is silently bypassed for non-SSE responses, and even when it fires it produces an infinite silent retry loop. The #135 watcher nudge is the only mechanism that can recover the agent.**\n\n---\n\n### (1) CONFIG PROPAGATION — CONFIRMED working (not the problem)\n\n- Both hung sessions loaded `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` at launch:\n  - K6yV (#138): `run=6ca2dfaa` loaded it at `06:01:17.541Z`\n  - OZWZ (#142): `run=aa5f8503` loaded it at `05:57:20.069Z`\n  - Config mtime = `04:59:53` → the chunkTimeout keys were present at both launches.\n- Launch chain works: crosslink kickoff → tmux → `claude` wrapper (`~/.local/bin/claude` bash) → `exec systemd-run --scope --user ... opencode run` → opencode 1.18.11 reads `Global.Path.config` = `OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR ?? XDG_CONFIG_HOME/opencode ?? ~/.config/opencode` (config.ts `globalConfigFile()`: config.json → opencode.json → opencode.jsonc). The wrapper only sets `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`; HOME/XDG_CONFIG_HOME survive tmux+systemd-run. `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` is irrelevant to opencode — **0 occurrences in the opencode binary** (verified via strings), and the wrapper never sets it for opencode anyway.\n\n### (2) HONORING — chunkTimeout IS implemented, but with a critical content-type guard\n\nSource: `packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts` (v1.18.11 confirmed identical in the installed binary):\n\n- `wrapSSE(res, ms, ctl)` — per-chunk SSE read timeout. **Guard at top:**\n  ```ts\n  if (!res.headers.get(\"content-type\")?.includes(\"text/event-stream\")) return res\n  ```\n  If the response content-type does not contain `text/event-stream`, the response is returned UNWRAPPED and **chunkTimeout is completely disabled**.\n- `resolveSDK` (line ~1738): `chunkTimeout`/`headerTimeout` are extracted from provider options and wired into a custom `fetch` wrapper; overall `timeout` is added as `AbortSignal.timeout` to the request signal.\n- `opencode-go` (models.dev: `npm:\"@ai-sdk/openai-compatible\", api:\"https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1\"`) goes through the same wrapper — so the mechanism is per-provider honored, **when the content-type matches**.\n\n### (3) REPRODUCTION — controlled minimal test (fake hanging SSE server, chunkTimeout=3000)\n\nThree server modes against `opencode run --model hangtest/hang-model`:\n\n| Server behavior | chunkTimeout=3000 behavior | ERROR entries | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| headers + `text/event-stream`, then hang | **fires** (abort ~3s) → AI SDK retries w/ exp backoff (gaps 3.5/5/7/11/19/33s) | **0** | silent infinite retry loop, process alive → killed only by outer `timeout` (EXIT=124) |\n| headers + `application/json`, then hang | **never fires** (wrapSSE guard bypass) — 2 POSTs then total silence | **0** | infinite hang, zero retries |\n| no headers at all | headerTimeout fires (2000ms) | **4** (ProviderHeaderTimeoutError) | retries + visible errors — this case IS protected |\n\nThe **application/json row exactly reproduces the real OZWZ signature**: last stream 06:01:26, then **zero retry streams and zero errors for 10.9h**. If chunkTimeout had fired at 300s in reality, the log would show retry streams every ~5min+backoff. It shows none → **chunkTimeout never fired in the real hang**.\n\n### (4) WHY — and what would actually protect\n\n**Root cause**: the real upstream response (or an intermediate) arrives with a content-type that does NOT include `text/event-stream`, so `wrapSSE` returns the response unwrapped and chunkTimeout is a no-op. The overall `timeout` (`AbortSignal.timeout` on the request) also fails to abort the already-resolved response body read in this path — the body reader hangs forever with no deadline. Result: last 'stream' never returns, zero ERROR, process alive, pane frozen, flags RUNNING — the exact reported signature.\n\n**What protects**:\n1. **#135 watcher nudge is the only currently-effective recovery** — but note the watchdog only sends `tmux send-keys \"continue working\"` and gives up after `max_nudges=5` (launch.rs `build_watchdog_script`), which will NOT unblock a hung stream promise. It needs to become a **kill/restart** (`tmux kill-session` + relaunch) once staleness exceeds a threshold.\n2. **Client-side**: apply the per-read deadline to ALL response bodies, not just `text/event-stream` — i.e. remove/relax the content-type guard in `wrapSSE` so a hanging body aborts regardless of header type. This is an opencode source change (not config).\n3. **Config-side (limited)**: `headerTimeout` already protects the no-headers case (proven). `chunkTimeout` only helps when the upstream genuinely returns SSE. No config value fixes the content-type bypass.\n4. **Operational**: the kickoff outer `timeout` (e.g. 30m/45m) eventually kills the process — but that's hours-long and the flag lies as RUNNING meanwhile.\n\n**Exact recommendation**: (a) patch opencode `wrapSSE` to drop the `text/event-stream` content-type guard (or add a general body-read deadline) so chunkTimeout covers all responses; (b) upgrade the #135 watcher from nudge to kill-and-restart after N stale checks; (c) keep headerTimeout as-is. Config alone cannot protect this failure mode.","created_at":"2026-08-03T18:11:07.120939434Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:fmLzQ5FXIztSEmsIH9qJZbpnPkgYSIkTl4JepA/OauE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgt+/Xfi/pqw4EWd/WlHR/LiU5R4t7k+H5zYx8tl1YnFwAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAleWjDDagLO7nbtJHyNhfJ7q/yq9RD7/lCVMkRIBFtu+b4HkTswLBXPDDY+QLmkGaqFY6PGFK6u7F9ZUSs8yKAw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:fmLzQ5FXIztSEmsIH9qJZbpnPkgYSIkTl4JepA/OauE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgt+/Xfi/pqw4EWd/WlHR/LiU5R4t7k+H5zYx8tl1YnFwAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFvZF5mwVqnVyxw3rSrKGtlw3vCeC7gxRrB6bOpY3mZ122gE80oo3vIOujnNGxjgfnvYgbNP0Ci2qz1HjZmGJg8="}
